{"id":114720,"title":"PDF Interactive Isosurface Ray Tracing of Large Octree Volumes","url":"https://www.sci.utah.edu/~knolla/octiso-rt06.pdf","final_url":"https://www.sci.utah.edu/~knolla/octiso-rt06.pdf","year":null,"kind":"web","source":"ddg","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"cdb6862c637165277d212c50bf3e6488f302b1013bbda2127cfe590787936aca","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793235732.1157331,"text_chars":51684,"abstract":"Xinghui Zhong\n\nhttps://www.sci.utah.edu › ~knolla › octiso-rt06.pdf\n\nPDF Interactive Isosurface Ray Tracing of Large Octree Volumes\nABSTRACT We present a technique for ray tracing isosurfaces of large compressed structured volumes. Data is first converted into a lossless-compression octree representation that occupies a fraction of the original memory footprint. An isosurface is then dynamically rendered by tracing rays through a min/max hierarchy inside interior octree nodes. By embedding the acceleration tree and scalar ...","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://www.sci.utah.edu/~knolla/octiso-rt06.pdf"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1978-octree-build.md","name":"Octree Build","k":2},{"path":"1590-bottom-up-octree-construction.md","name":"Bottom-up Octree Construction","k":5},{"path":"1978-octree-volume-structure.md","name":"Octree Volume Structure","k":2},{"path":"1890-ray-octree-traversal-gargantini-and-atkinson-variant.md","name":"Ray-Octree Traversal (Gargantini and Atkinson variant)","k":3},{"path":"2076-point-location.md","name":"Point Location","k":2},{"path":"1822-cell-retrieval-via-neighbor-finding.md","name":"Cell Retrieval via Neighbor-Finding","k":2},{"path":"1739-octree-traversal-with-min-max-pruning.md","name":"Octree Traversal with Min/Max Pruning","k":3},{"path":"1979-octree-volume-compression.md","name":"Octree Volume Compression","k":2},{"path":"2198-neighbor-finding.md","name":"Neighbor Finding","k":1},{"path":"1994-scalar-leaf-traversal.md","name":"Scalar Leaf Traversal","k":2},{"path":"2013-ray-octree-traversal-gargantini-and-atkinson-variant-cap-nod.md","name":"Ray-Octree Traversal (Gargantini and Atkinson variant) > Cap Node Traversal","k":1},{"path":"2020-min-max-tree-construction-with-forward-neighbors.md","name":"Min/Max Tree Construction with Forward Neighbors","k":1},{"path":"2241-lambertian-shading-with-packet-architecture.md","name":"Lambertian Shading with Packet Architecture","k":2},{"path":"1841-ray-traversal-of-octree-nodes.md","name":"Ray Traversal of Octree Nodes","k":3},{"path":"2240-voxel-cell-duality-mapping.md","name":"Voxel-Cell Duality Mapping","k":2},{"path":"2213-trilinear-isosurface-intersection.md","name":"Trilinear Isosurface Intersection","k":4},{"path":"2232-time-variant-volume-rendering-with-octrees.md","name":"Time-Variant Volume Rendering with Octrees","k":2},{"path":"3003-cap-node-traversal.md","name":"Cap Node Traversal","k":1}]}